          <p><em>Last reviewed: June 2026</em></p>

          <h2>Summary</h2>
          <p>I do not collect, store, or process any personal data directly. This website uses a small number of third-party services that may process your IP address as part of normal web operation. No analytics or tracking are performed.</p>

          <h2>Who I am</h2>
          <p>
            CodesThings.com is the personal website of James Macmillan.<br />
            Contact: <a href="mailto:james@codesthings.com">james@codesthings.com</a><br />
            Phone: +44 7736 667 115
          </p>

          <h2>What data is processed and by whom</h2>
          <p>I do not directly collect or store personal data. The following third-party services are used to operate the site and may process your IP address:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — hosts this website. GitHub may log IP addresses per their <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — fonts are loaded from Google's servers. Google may process your IP address per their <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>jsDelivr CDN</strong> — icons are loaded from jsDelivr's CDN. jsDelivr may log requests per their <a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The source code for this website is publicly available at <a href="https://github.com/jamescodesthings/jamescodesthings.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">github.com/jamescodesthings/jamescodesthings.github.io</a>.</p>

          <h2>Legal basis</h2>
          <p>Third-party service processing described above is carried out on the basis of legitimate interests in operating a functional, accessible website (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).</p>

          <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
          <p>Please see the <a href="/about-cookies">About Cookies</a> page.</p>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to: access your personal data; rectification of inaccurate data; erasure; restriction of processing; data portability; and to object to processing. To exercise rights relating to third-party processing, please contact those services directly.</p>

          <h2>Right to complain</h2>
          <p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a> if you believe your data has been handled unlawfully.</p>
